{"task": "Revise your contribution. Preserve supported positions, correct omissions, and identify any relevant issue still open.", "evidence": {"MAIN": "Security Council meeting S/PV.9771, 31 October 2024. The United States draft S/2024/796 was adopted as resolution 2756 (2024), with 12 votes in favour, zero against, two abstentions (Mozambique and the Russian Federation), and one member not participating (Algeria).", "AMEND": "Algeria proposed S/2024/797, which would note nine consecutive years without an OHCHR visit, and S/2024/798, which would have the Council consider expanding MINURSO's mandate to monitor, help investigate, report on and follow up on humanitarian-law and human-rights violations. They received 6–0–9 and 5–0–10 respectively and neither secured enough votes to be adopted.", "TEXT": "Resolution 2756 extended the MINURSO mandate until 31 October 2025 and urged increased cooperation with OHCHR, including facilitating visits. The proposed language to consider adding monitoring functions was not incorporated.", "DZ-A": "Speaking for Algeria, Bendjama introduced two amendments concerning human rights. He cited the report documenting the ninth consecutive year without an OHCHR visit and argued that MINURSO should have a human-rights monitoring component, as other missions do.", "DZ-B": "After voting, Bendjama explained Algeria's deliberate non-participation on the final resolution and said the penholder had disregarded Algeria's views. He reaffirmed that the Sahrawi people should be free to choose their future."}, "drafts": [{"id": "western-sahara-minurso-2024-10-31/common/opening_1", "text": "Based on the evidence provided, here is the analysis of the material position and concern of the Algerian delegation:

**Material Position:**
The Algerian delegation firmly opposed the adoption of Resolution 2756 (2024) without incorporating specific human rights monitoring mechanisms. Their core position was that the Security Council must address the systemic failure of the Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights"}]}
